{"id":"word:hebrew:H5983","type":"word","title":"עַמּוֹן","subtitle":"H5983 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Ammon , a son of Lot; also his posterity and their country","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עַמּוֹן (H5983) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 106 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עַמּוֹן (ʻAmmôwn) means Ammon , a son of Lot; also his posterity and their country First listed occurrence: 1Chr 18 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עַמּוֹן","transliteration":"ʻAmmôwn","pronunciation":"am-mone'","strong":"H5983","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5983","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["עַמּ֔וֹן","עַמּֽוֹן","עַמּ֖וֹן","עַמּ֑וֹן","עַמּ֜וֹן"],"morphs":[["HNp",105],["HC/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Ammon , a son of Lot; also his posterity and their country","usage":"Ammon, Ammonites.","full":"H5983. Ammon עַמּוֺן 106 proper name, of a people Ammon , ᵐ5 Αμμαν , Αμμων (Assyrian Bît Ammanu COT Glossary ); always (except 1Sam 11:11 [where however ᵐ5 reads ע ׳בְּנֵי ], Psa 83:8 , which have ׳ע alone) עַמּוֺן בְּנֵי , connected by J with בֶּןעַֿמִּי son of Lot Gen 19:38 (and meaning of name doubtless sought herein by J; compare II. עַם ); people apparently akin to Israel, but usually hostile, dwelling east of Jordan, northeast of Moab, between Arnon and Jabbok: Num 21:24 (twice in verse) (JE), Deut 2:19 (twice in verse); 2:37 ; 3:11 , 16 ; Josh 12:2 ; 13:10 (D), 13:25 (P), Judg 3:13 ; 10:6 25t. Judges 10-12, 1Sam 11:11 ; 12:12 ; 14:47 ; 2Sam 8:12 ; 10:1 14 t. 2 Samuel 10-12; 17:27 ; 1Kin 11:7 , 33 ; 2Kin 23:13 ; 24:2 ; 1Chr 18:11 20t. Chronicles, Amos 1:13 ; Isa 11:14 ; Jer 9:25 9 t. Jeremiah, Zeph 2:8-9 , Ezek 21:25 ; Ezekiel 21:33 5 t. Ezekiel 25; Dan 11:41 . &#8212; See Che Ammon in Ency. Bib .","rootNote":"from 5971 ; tribal, i.e. inbred;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver